{"id": "EUVD-2026-82036", "enisaUuid": "ecc457df-022e-314c-aaad-c46fe9e471dd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: fix non-AQL packet accounting for MLO stations\n\n__mt76_tx_queue_skb() overrides the wcid passed by the driver with\nsta->drv_priv, so the wcid might incorrectly be changed after TX,\ncausing wcid->non_aql_packets to be counted on the wrong wcid. For\nexample, on the AP side, if a station's setup link is the 5G link and\nthe station uses 2G to transmit a frame, the value of non_aql_packets\nis increased on the 5G wcid but decreased on the 2G wcid. Once the\ninflated counter exceeds MT_MAX_NON_AQL_PKT, the TX scheduler\npermanently refuses to service the station.\n\nDrop the reassignment and account on the wcid used for transmission.\nThis also records the actual wcid in the queue entry.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c321f86846ead00552bc65f73f5b5f1f81d4023", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f85f6933cc170155f1c7c2dffdd014965787c71b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc7fae55255ccbde009232e84b102d2782a69ecf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/186c957ac3325aefb982567ffdd3654b283688a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ae659743ba936b22ecb4620815887728e2820d6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90375", "GHSA-c2f5-4c4q-2g8j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00b8bbe4-8f89-3b0f-8d86-efd61e5cb786", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1378e5228aaa1bf6bb253a379c7de1722a94e00 <2c321f86846ead00552bc65f73f5b5f1f81d4023"}, {"id": "3c9a2d94-e2f8-3afc-a70d-757f3d54dfe7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1378e5228aaa1bf6bb253a379c7de1722a94e00 <f85f6933cc170155f1c7c2dffdd014965787c71b"}, {"id": "4034d132-a5cd-3281-b689-ae3b1d8ff885", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "4cef31dd-4eda-396c-9b31-258fb36970bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5440e3d7-9307-39ae-96b9-98f2451f33ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1378e5228aaa1bf6bb253a379c7de1722a94e00 <fc7fae55255ccbde009232e84b102d2782a69ecf"}, {"id": "8107b237-6473-358a-a872-418c1155011d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "ca0f1851-baaa-30ae-b0e9-e50e4b0fa6c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10"}, {"id": "cb4cd693-a7e4-31c8-b7c7-9cb3b6711e25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1378e5228aaa1bf6bb253a379c7de1722a94e00 <186c957ac3325aefb982567ffdd3654b283688a7"}, {"id": "cef85c5d-c529-39ed-9bd9-a2ae157e511c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "dd26e3c2-bfe5-3cb5-b651-50a5082a29db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e1378e5228aaa1bf6bb253a379c7de1722a94e00 <8ae659743ba936b22ecb4620815887728e2820d6"}, {"id": "ec4fab01-8b75-324f-837b-7615a1228781", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "fdf1c237-2c60-3180-854d-c0023d4cbe80", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b654f7d5-682a-3334-b2ea-c02bc4ba2260", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}